    "q-276367": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276367",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<2.17).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9798\\,$ | $\\,0.9803\\,$ | $\\,0.9808\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9842\\,$ | $\\,0.9846\\,$ | $\\,0.9850\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,0.9881\\,$ | $\\,0.9884\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<2.17)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<2.17)=P(Z\\le 2.17)=Φ(2.17).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/c1d8ba1ea5e9b0362fa59a5993e4292dde7b4dd8a8694c71f9dbec026fa3e821.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(2.17)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $2.1$ and the column that corresponds to $0.07.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9798\\,$ | $\\,0.9803\\,$ | $\\,0.9808\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9842\\,$ | $\\,0.9846\\,$ | $\\,0.9850\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,0.9881\\,$ | $\\,0.9884\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.17)=Φ(2.17)=0.9850.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
