    "q-330874": {
      "dom_id": "step-q330874",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-1.94).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0207\\,$ | $\\,0.0202\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0268\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ | $\\,0.0256\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ | $\\,0.0322\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<-1.94)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<-1.94)=P(Z\\le -1.94)=Φ(-1.94).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/8e2fd49cb0a74c1741c8155d50be56e5c002d7a0ed21adb5b49d2cc26ebbb24d.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(-1.94)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $-1.9$ and the column that corresponds to $0.04.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0207\\,$ | $\\,0.0202\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0268\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ | $\\,0.0256\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ | $\\,0.0322\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le -1.94)=Φ(-1.94)=0.0262.\n$$",
